commit(n,t,ds,ch,items,'A diagram of exterior and divided powers is followed by rank formulas and Pascal-type expansions for a translation operator. The shift is defined with the variable mu, not H’s capital N. The rank argument uses square-bracket indices [N]; its final prime/closing-parenthesis stroke is not secure. A prime on the first Phi of the bottom-left diagram is visible and retained, although the adjacent Psi has no separate prime. The continuation marks are horizontal strokes, not printed ellipses; the rank products and binomial recurrence identify their continuation role, so they are not interpreted as subtraction in the notes. The margin’s second step has N+p-2 and stops at +2 phi. The general tau expansion follows from the written recurrence tau phi_r=phi_r+phi_(r-1) by the binomial theorem for the identity and lowering operators; this supports the continuation reading but does not license filling missing terms. The cancelled polynomial trial and several cancelled coefficients remain partly uncertain. Foot number 338.',hand=['On this leaf capital N is angular and tall, while the shift variable mu has a left descender and low hump. H’s N in that definition loses this distinction.','Stars below Phi/Psi can have downward tails; a dark terminal part of the Psi arm is not automatically a prime. Phi at the bottom-left does have a detached prime.','Continuation is repeatedly written with dashes, including a lone dash before a terminal plus. H normalizes these to ellipses.','The oblique equivalence-like sign uses a bent/wavy stroke beside one straight stroke; its exact identity remains marked rather than silently regularized.'],notation=[('tau','Translation (tau P)(mu)=P(mu+1).'),('phi_r','Lowering recurrence tau phi_r=phi_r+phi_(r-1); looped phi with long descending stem.'),('[N]','Square-bracket evaluation indices under Phi and Psi.'),('c_pq','Lower-case coefficient in rank and lower exterior-power expressions.')],abbr=[('rg','rang'),('fact.','facteurs'),('mono','monomorphisme')],checks=[check('337-text-diagram','Diagram and claimed mono label transcribed; no monomorphism proof checked.'),check('337-text-ranks','Factorial and binomial rank expressions carried as written.'),check('337-translation-binomial','Writing D phi_r=phi_(r-1), the displayed recurrence gives tau=1+D; expanding (1+D)^p yields the written binomial coefficients and final term. This is a conditional algebraic check of the expansion.','targeted proof check')],unresolved=[r'oblique simeq signs',r'S|section character',r'final rank prime or closing parenthesis',r'cancelled polynomial, plus, Ainsi, star, tau trials and p(p-1)/2'])
